<BaseLayout title="Reaction Time by Age – Why Charts Are Not a Diagnosis" description="Read how reaction time by age is discussed in public sources, why a browser five-round test is not an age ranking, and how to compare your own sessions instead.">
  <section class="article-hero"><div class="shell"><p class="eyebrow">Score context</p><h1>Reaction Time by Age</h1><p class="lede">Age-group charts describe group tendencies. They do not classify a visitor from one browser session.</p></div></section>
  <article class="article-page article-copy">
    <h2>What people mean by reaction time by age</h2>
    <p>Searches for reaction time by age usually want a table: teenagers, adults, and older adults on one axis, milliseconds on the other. Public summaries often say simple visual reaction time can slow across adulthood, while a well-slept 50-year-old can still beat a tired 20-year-old on a given day. That is a group pattern, not a personal grade.</p>
    <p>This site’s tool is a five-round visual click in a browser. Display refresh, input hardware, and JavaScript scheduling sit inside the number. An age chart from a laboratory task does not map one-to-one onto that result.</p>
    <h2>Why this page does not print a diagnostic table</h2>
    <p>A precise age table would need a cited study, a matching task, and a disclosed sample. This page will not invent one. If you need a clinical or occupational assessment, that belongs with a qualified test, not a free homepage tool.</p>
    <p>Use the <a href="/average-reaction-time/">average reaction time</a> guide for how this site’s best, median, and average are calculated. Use the homepage to generate a new five-round session under a stable setup.</p>
    <h2>A fair personal comparison</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Keep the same device, browser, and input method.</li>
      <li>Complete all five rounds instead of saving one lucky click.</li>
      <li>Compare your own sessions across days, not against an unsourced age chart.</li>
      <li>Note sleep, distractions, and whether you anticipated the green signal.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="article-callout">Run the live <a href="/">reaction time test</a> on the homepage. Method rules stay on the <a href="/reaction-time-test/">five-round explanation</a>.</p>
  </article>
